*> The confirm-delete screen (US16-1; 08 §10.8.6 confirm_delete texts): "Delete This World?", "<level
*> name> will be deleted for good", Delete and Cancel. Delete removes the selected world's folder
*> (WORLD-DELETE) and returns to the world list; Cancel returns to it with the world kept.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. CONFIRM-DELETE-BUILD.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, GUI width, GUI height.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CLARGS.
 01 WS-KIND                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ACTION              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-W                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 98.
 01 WS-H                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 20.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(80).
 01 WS-KEY-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(512).
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z1                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z2                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z3                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z4                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z5                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-GW                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-GH                   BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-GW L-GH.
     MOVE WK-LABEL TO WS-KIND
     COMPUTE WS-X = L-GW / 2 - 100
     MOVE 40 TO WS-Y
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.confirm_delete.title" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 38 TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-Z1 WS-X WS-Y WS-Z2 WS-Z3 WS-KEY
         WS-KEY-LENGTH
     MOVE 1 TO LA-COUNT
     MOVE WL-NAME(SM-SELECTED) TO LA-TEXT(1)
     MOVE WL-NAME-LENGTH(SM-SELECTED) TO LA-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.confirm_delete.text" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 37 TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "LANG-FORMAT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY WS-KEY-LENGTH LANG-ARGS WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 64 TO WS-Y
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-Z1 WS-Z2 WS-X WS-Y WS-Z3 WS-Z4 WS-TEXT
         WS-LENGTH WS-Z5
     MOVE WK-BUTTON TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 100 TO WS-Y
     MOVE ACT-CONFIRM-DELETE TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.confirm_delete.delete" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 39 TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-ACTION WS-X WS-Y WS-W WS-H WS-KEY
         WS-KEY-LENGTH
     ADD 102 TO WS-X
     MOVE ACT-SINGLE-PLAYER TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.common.cancel" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 31 TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-ACTION WS-X WS-Y WS-W WS-H WS-KEY
         WS-KEY-LENGTH
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM CONFIRM-DELETE-BUILD.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. CONFIRM-DELETE-DELETE.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE: Delete: the selected world's folder is deleted; the world list opens again
*> (read anew, nothing selected).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLCONST.
 01 WS-FOLDER              PIC X(80).
 01 WS-FOLDER-LENGTH       BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SCREEN              BINARY-LONG VALUE SCR-WORLD-LIST.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE.
     MOVE WL-FOLDER(SM-SELECTED) TO WS-FOLDER
     MOVE WL-FOLDER-LENGTH(SM-SELECTED) TO WS-FOLDER-LENGTH
     CALL "WORLD-DELETE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FOLDER WS-FOLDER-LENGTH
     CALL "SCREEN-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SCREEN
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM CONFIRM-DELETE-DELETE.
